## 9. Friends Engine (`components/friends`)

The **Friends Engine** orchestrates external CLI engines (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Kimi) for builds, secondary code reviews and adversarial audits, inside isolated Jujutsu child revisions or on a remote host.

### Friends or Sub-agents
All delegated work goes to a friend or a sub-agent. There are no workers and no managers. The agent chooses per task.
- **Friends do the heavy work**: long runs, builds, production work, anything that loads the machine. Run them on `atlas-worker-1` (`--host atlas-worker-1 --remote-cwd <dir>`), not on the laptop. The `friends` skill has the host rules.
- **Sub-agents do light work** (Claude Code only): research, a quick search, a small check. Use one when the task is short and the operator wants to see it in the sub-agents panel.

### Supported Friends & Models
- **Claude (`claude`)**: Anthropic Claude Code CLI (default `claude-opus-5-5`; Fable 5.1 runs only in the bug sweeper).
- **Lean Opus 4.5 (`lean-opus-4-5`)**: the `claude` CLI pinned to `claude-opus-4-5` with `--strict-mcp-config` (zero MCP servers). The writing model.
- **Codex (`codex`)**: OpenAI Codex CLI (`gpt-6-astra`, `gpt-5.6-sol`, `gpt-5.5`).
- **Kimi (`kimi`)**: Moonshot Kimi Code CLI (`kimi-k3`).
- **Grok (`grok`)**: xAI Grok Build CLI (`grok-4.6`, `grok-4.5`), `--reasoning-effort` supported.
- **OpenCode (`opencode`)**: open-weight runner (`deepseek-coder-v2`).

### Viewers (`harness/tools/viewers`)
Operator-facing HTML pages come from the shipped templates, never freestyled:
`node harness/tools/viewers/render.mjs --list` (bakeoff, report, sidebyside, tabs), then
`node harness/tools/viewers/render.mjs <template> <data.json> -o <out.html>`. Themed dark1, one
self-contained file, opened as file://. The `viewers` skill has the data shapes.

### Default Skills
The installer ships these skills into every seat, in both `.claude/skills/` (Claude Code) and `.agents/skills/` (Codex, OpenCode, agy): `brain-self-kickoff`, `context-load`, `brain-session-end`, `viewers`, `opus-writer`, `world-class-hooks`, `friends`, `bug-sweeper`. Voice packs ship to `data/opus-writer/voice-pack/`. Harness-shipped skills are overwritten on every install; skills a seat adds itself are left alone. Sources live in `components/harness/skills/` and `components/brain/skills/`.

### Long Runs Have No Clock
A friend run has **no timer** unless the caller sets one. `friend run` and `dispatchFriend` default to none; `--timeout 0` (or less) also means none. A timer that fires mid-job kills the agent with no report, and the next agent inherits half-done code.
- A live orchestrator watches the age of each run and decides by judgement when one has gone on too long.
- Set a timer only for a quick call: a probe (`--timeout 60000`), a short second opinion.
- A run that a timer cut fails loudly with "timed out ... the work is NOT finished". A run cut from outside is **resumed in the same workspace**. It is never read as a verdict.

### Key Capabilities
1. **Isolated Jujutsu Child Revisions (`jj new`)**: Dispatches run in an isolated working copy without dirtying the parent agent's workspace.
2. **Credential Multi-Tenant Sandbox**: Injects OAuth tokens and provider configurations dynamically from `~/.config/incubator/max-tokens.env` or local auth pools.
3. **Non-Interactive & CLI Execution**:
   ```bash
   # List available friends and active accounts
   node harness/components/friends/tools/friend.mjs catalog
   node harness/components/friends/tools/friend.mjs accounts list

   # Dispatch a prompt to a Friend
   node harness/components/friends/tools/friend.mjs dispatch claude "Review API error handling in routes/docs.mjs"
   node harness/components/friends/tools/friend.mjs dispatch codex "Implement constant-time timingSafeEqual helper" --model gpt-6-astra
   ```
4. **Remote hosts (`--host <ssh-alias> --remote-cwd <dir>`)**: a Claude friend runs on another machine over ssh. The prompt, system prompt and token go over stdin; a watchdog on the host kills the run when ssh dies; there is no jj isolation. The seat sets up the host and its folders, one folder per concurrent run. The `friends` skill ("Remote hosts") has the setup.

